     8| *   2. A single-flight WORKER drains the queue and runs the real end-to-end
     9| *      execution pipeline already implemented in `ivx-senior-developer-runtime`:
    10| *      repo read → file create/modify → tests → typecheck → build → commit →
    11| *      push → Render deploy → poll deploy → verify /health + /version.
    12| *   3. Every job's verifiable result is recorded in a durable PROOF LEDGER
    13| *      (Supabase-backed, survives Render's diskless restarts; in-memory fallback
    14| *      for local/test).
    15| *
    16| * HTTP 409 FIX (2026-07-17):
    17| *   - Per-owner single-flight: only one active task per owner at a time.
    18| *   - Duplicate requests ATTACH to the running job (return its jobId) instead
    19| *     of returning HTTP 409.
    20| *   - Stale jobs auto-expire after a configurable timeout.
    21| *   - Cancel Job and Resume Job endpoints.
    22| *   - Granular stage tracking: QUEUED → RUNNING → PATCHING → TESTING →
    23| *     COMMITTING → DEPLOYING → VERIFYING → COMPLETED/FAILED.
    24| *   - Live Work updated in real time with current stage and progress.
    25| *   - The user's request is NEVER discarded — it is queued or attached.
